# Language policy

## Default split

| Layer | Language | Examples |
|-------|----------|----------|
| **App UI (chrome)** | **English only** | Screen titles, buttons, settings labels, errors, clinic link strip, website portal |
| **Coach & meals** | **User language** (`userLanguage` in TargetService) | Gemini chat, coach card, meal `name_local`, quick questions, AI rules text |
| **Exported documents** | **User language** | Visit report HTML body, clinical narrative in exports |

Do **not** add `langCode === 'he'` (or other locale) branches to new UI components. Pass `userLanguage` / `lang` only into AI prompts, meal parsing, chat, and export **content** builders.

## Settings UX

The dashboard language picker controls **coach & meals language**, not full app localization. Prefer copy like “Coach & meals language” over a generic “Language” label when touching that control.

## RTL

Hebrew/Arabic still need correct text direction in **user-content areas** (chat bubbles, meal lists, exported HTML) even when chrome stays English LTR.

## Intent detection

Chat slash commands and natural-language triggers may stay multilingual (`chatIntent.ts`) — that is input parsing, not UI chrome.

## When to revisit

Full UI i18n (react-i18next or similar) is a later milestone if mass-market users cannot use English settings. Until then, keep chrome English and localize generated content only.
